<Project>

  <!--
    Package identity for the two projects a plugin builds against. Everything else in the solution
    inherits these harmlessly, because only KHost.Abstractions and KHost.Common set IsPackable.

    The version here is the *contract* version, and it is the host's runtime gate. A plugin needs the
    KHost.Abstractions version recorded in its .deps.json; a host runs it only on the same major and
    no older than that (Common/Plugins/ContractsVersion). So a major is how a break is signalled: a
    removal, a changed signature, a member without a default body on an extension point, a changed
    enum value. A minor is an addition; a patch a fix in KHost.Common with no change of shape.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ContractsVersion>1.0.0</ContractsVersion>
    <!--
      The assembly version is pinned and the package version is not, because they answer to
      different people. A plugin's compiled reference binds to this number, so moving it makes
      every plugin already in the wild fail to load — which is exactly what happened the first time
      these were packed: KHost.Plugins.Spotify bound to 1.0.0.0, the host served 0.1.0.0, and its
      break-music provider silently vanished with one line in the log.

      So it does not move at all, not even on a new major. The contracts version is the host's real
      compatibility gate, and it is checked against a plugin's .deps.json before a single assembly is
      bound, so an incompatible plugin is refused with a message a host can act on rather than failing
      to load for a reason nobody can read. Moving this as well would only replace that message with
      the outage above. ContractsVersion goes on the package, the file version and the assembly's
      metadata, where the host reads its own.
    -->
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>$(ContractsVersion).0</FileVersion>
    <Authors>Michael Riddle</Authors>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/riddlemd/KHost</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
